{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781410021689,"sessionID":"ses_13bb08173ffeCrsry0l92MOWEw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_tzKelfenZ2m9LWAKVKt49O4l","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/output_contract.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/output_contract.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deliverable Contract\n2: \n3: Create an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n4: \n5: ## `answer/initial_room_plan.md`\n6: \n7: Record the room assignment plan before any coordinator update is introduced.\n8: \n9: Required facts:\n10: \n11: - One row or entry for every session in `02_sessions.csv`.\n12: - The selected room for each session.\n13: - The room evidence that supports each assignment: capacity, time block, required equipment or room trait, and cost.\n14: - The initial total room cost and budget status against the `$800` ceiling.\n15: - Any backup room considered for a fragile assignment.\n16: \n17: ## `answer/update_response.md`\n18: \n19: After the coordinator update is introduced, explain what changed and how the plan should be repaired.\n20: \n21: Required facts:\n22: \n23: - The update source and date.\n24: - The specific room assignment affected by the update.\n25: - Which original assignments remain valid and should be preserved.\n26: - The replacement assignment and why it satisfies the same session requirements.\n27: - The revised cost effect.\n28: \n29: ## `answer/final_room_plan.md`\n30: \n31: Write the final room assignment package after applying the update.\n32: \n33: Required facts:\n34: \n35: - One final room assignment for every session.\n36: - The final total room cost and remaining budget.\n37: - A short note confirming the same workshop objective is still covered.\n38: - A short note naming preserved work from the initial plan.\n39: \n40: Rules:\n41: \n42: - Use local files only.\n43: - Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n44: - Do not relax hard room requirements unless a local file explicitly says to.\n45: - Extra scratch files are allowed, but the three named deliverables under `answer/` are the review packet.\n\n(End of file - total 45 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/initial_room_plan.md`\n\nRecord the room assignment plan before any coordinator update is introduced.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every session in `02_sessions.csv`.\n- The selected room for each session.\n- The room evidence that supports each assignment: capacity, time block, required equipment or room trait, and cost.\n- The initial total room cost and budget status against the `$800` ceiling.\n- Any backup room considered for a fragile assignment.\n\n## `answer/update_response.md`\n\nAfter the coordinator update is introduced, explain what changed and how the plan should be repaired.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/output_contract.md","text":"# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/initial_room_plan.md`\n\nRecord the room assignment plan before any coordinator update is introduced.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every session in `02_sessions.csv`.\n- The selected room for each session.\n- The room evidence that supports each assignment: capacity, time block, required equipment or room trait, and cost.\n- The initial total room cost and budget status against the `$800` ceiling.\n- Any backup room considered for a fragile assignment.\n\n## `answer/update_response.md`\n\nAfter the coordinator update is introduced, explain what changed and how the plan should be repaired.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The update source and date.\n- The specific room assignment affected by the update.\n- Which original assignments remain valid and should be preserved.\n- The replacement assignment and why it satisfies the same session requirements.\n- The revised cost effect.\n\n## `answer/final_room_plan.md`\n\nWrite the final room assignment package after applying the update.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One final room assignment for every session.\n- The final total room cost and remaining budget.\n- A short note confirming the same workshop objective is still covered.\n- A short note naming preserved work from the initial plan.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Do not relax hard room requirements unless a local file explicitly says to.\n- Extra scratch files are allowed, but the three named deliverables under `answer/` are the review packet.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":45,"totalLines":45,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/community_workshop_replan/output_contract.md","time":{"start":1781410021634,"end":1781410021679}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_03b115fc313d0921016a2e28e57ec48191a751ce76500539fd"}},"id":"prt_ec44fc0fc001FGnD2HGALvOahL","sessionID":"ses_13bb08173ffeCrsry0l92MOWEw","messageID":"msg_ec44fa2e90011J6BVGV6pnQfJy"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781410021689,"sessionID":"ses_13bb08173ffeCrsry0l92MOWEw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_Xr8TCUcshA0f8DlAqgmOnInT","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/01_planning_rules.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/01_planning_rules.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Planning Rules\n2: \n3: Effective date: 2026-06-03\n4: \n5: ## Source Reliability\n6: \n7: - Use the newest dated facility source for room availability when facility notes conflict.\n8: - Session requirements in `02_sessions.csv` control capacity, time block, equipment, and room-trait needs.\n9: - Room traits and base costs come from `03_room_options.csv` unless a newer facility update changes room availability.\n10: \n11: ## Hard Requirements\n12: \n13: - Assign every session to exactly one room.\n14: - Use rooms that are available for the session time block.\n15: - Room capacity must be at least the session attendee count.\n16: - If a session needs a projector, demo table, quiet room, or loading access, the assigned room must provide it.\n17: - Total room cost must be at or below `$800`.\n18: - Prefer the lowest-cost valid room for each session unless preserving a correct existing assignment after an update is more important.\n19: \n20: ## Replanning Rule\n21: \n22: If a coordinator update makes part of the initial plan invalid, repair only the affected part when possible. Preserve correct assignments that still satisfy all requirements.\n\n(End of file - total 22 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Planning Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-06-03\n\n## Source Reliability\n\n- Use the newest dated facility source for room availability when facility notes conflict.\n- Session requirements in `02_sessions.csv` control capacity, time block, equipment, and room-trait needs.\n- Room traits and base costs come from `03_room_options.csv` unless a newer facility update changes room availability.\n\n## Hard Requirements\n\n- Assign every session to exactly one room.\n- Use rooms that are available for the session time block.\n- Room capacity must be at least the session attendee count.\n- If a session needs a projector, demo table, quiet room, or loading access, the assigned room must provide it.\n- Total room cost must be at or below `$800`.\n- Prefer the lowest-cost valid room for each session unless preserving a correct existing assignment after an update is more important.\n\n## Replanning Rule","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/01_planning_rules.md","text":"# Planning Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-06-03\n\n## Source Reliability\n\n- Use the newest dated facility source for room availability when facility notes conflict.\n- Session requirements in `02_sessions.csv` control capacity, time block, equipment, and room-trait needs.\n- Room traits and base costs come from `03_room_options.csv` unless a newer facility update changes room availability.\n\n## Hard Requirements\n\n- Assign every session to exactly one room.\n- Use rooms that are available for the session time block.\n- Room capacity must be at least the session attendee count.\n- If a session needs a projector, demo table, quiet room, or loading access, the assigned room must provide it.\n- Total room cost must be at or below `$800`.\n- Prefer the lowest-cost valid room for each session unless preserving a correct existing assignment after an update is more important.\n\n## Replanning Rule\n\nIf a coordinator update makes part of the initial plan invalid, repair only the affected part when possible. Preserve correct assignments that still satisfy all requirements.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":22,"totalLines":22,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/community_workshop_replan/01_planning_rules.md","time":{"start":1781410021644,"end":1781410021683}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_03b115fc313d0921016a2e28e57ee08191a9136481300e30e6"}},"id":"prt_ec44fc109001OMhstOnxP1d3m5","sessionID":"ses_13bb08173ffeCrsry0l92MOWEw","messageID":"msg_ec44fa2e90011J6BVGV6pnQfJy"}}
